From d6fad8bb720e7caaf6b043097dd2db870afab788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:24:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] worker store: re-send an unknown receipt inside the
 same call, never on a later write

Review of PR #2490 (5895917777, request changes at 1f5d8eba2e): deferring the resend of a
timed-out entry to the NEXT write committed transcript rows twice. The caller of a timed-out
transcript.append got the exception, session_persistence._db_flush_write stamps no markers on
failure, so the next flush re-collected rows A; the next _apply first re-sent the stalled seq N
(A) and then appended seq N+1 (A+B). The owner has no uid dedupe for such rows: A landed twice.
The resend's result (row annotations) was also discarded.

- runtime_session_store._persist_resending: on an unknown outcome (worker_receipt_timeout, a
  closed owner link) the SAME call re-sends the same entry under its own sequence and returns
  the real result. _RETRYABLE_ATTEMPTS=2 sends bound the wait at 2x the 90 s receipt budget,
  inside the turn lease's remaining authority at a refresh. Exhaustion latches as a sticky
  WorkerPersistenceError exactly as before the PR (a latched store sends nothing more), so a
  re-flushing caller can never duplicate. Refusals, lost_receipt, outbox_full: unchanged.
- Drops the cross-call state (_unknown, _resume_unknown, _note_unknown) and, with it, the
  turn_facade_lease and runtime_session_child changes: the store no longer surfaces a raw
  retryable error to the lease, and close() is back to the base rule.
- Log wording (review nit): "worker receipt outcome recovered after Ns (op=..., sends=N)",
  covering closed-link recoveries too.

Tests: tests/agent/test_runtime_session_store_receipt_timeout.py, 13 passed; on 1f5d8eba2e's
code 8 fail, including the exactly-once append test (A, B committed once each) and the
exhausted re-flush test. 57 files importing the store/lease/child: 473 passed. 7 mutants
(retry classification, send bound, in-call resend, sticky conversion, log guard,
ConnectionClosed) all killed.
